.TH MU2EDAQ\-DOWNTIME\-LOGGER 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-downtime-logger 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger \- detect and record Mu2e DAQ downtime events
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger
.RB { \-c | \-\-config }
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-log\-level
.IR LEVEL ]
.br
.B mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger
.B \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger
is a PySide6 desktop application.
It runs a set of pluggable
.I detectors
(ZeroMQ, UDP, SOAP, disk activity, log file), each on its own
.BR QThread ,
and folds their UP/DOWN/UNKNOWN readings into one weighted score:
.PP
.RS
.nf
score = sum(weight of DOWN detectors) / sum(weight of UP or DOWN detectors)
.fi
.RE
.PP
UNKNOWN detectors abstain.
When the score reaches
.I trip_threshold
and stays there for
.I debounce_seconds
a downtime event is opened, written to the storage backend, and a
non-modal popup asks the shifter for category, subsystem, cause and notes.
The event is closed automatically once the score is at or below
.I clear_threshold
for
.IR debounce_seconds .
Thresholds, weights and detectors come from the YAML file named by
.BR \-\-config ;
see
.BR mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.yaml (5).
.PP
.B Monitoring starts disabled.
Detectors run and the score is displayed, but no event is opened until the
shifter switches
.I Monitoring
on in the main window or the tray menu.
There is no configuration key or option that changes this.
.PP
The main window shows the live detector table and score above a history
table of recorded events.
Double\-click a row to edit it; the context menu offers
.IR Edit ,
.I End downtime now
(only for the event the state machine currently holds open),
.I Delete event
(permanent) and
.IR "New event" .
Closing the window leaves the application running in the system tray.
.PP
If
.B webserver.enabled
is true, a read\-only HTTP view (Python
.BR http.server ,
one thread per request) is started on
.BR webserver.bind : webserver.port
and the application announces itself to
.BR mu2edaq\-discover (1)
when the
.B mu2edaq_discovery
package is importable.
The routes are documented in
.BR mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger\-api (7).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
YAML configuration file.
Required; there is no default path and no search path.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-level " LEVEL"
Python logging level for the root logger: one of
.BR DEBUG ,
.BR INFO ,
.BR WARNING ,
.BR ERROR .
Default
.BR INFO .
Log records go to standard error.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config/config.example.yaml
Five\-detector example.
Its ZeroMQ and SOAP detectors point at the placeholder host
.IR daq01 ,
which does not resolve; see
.BR mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.yaml (5).
.TP
.I config/local.yaml
Three\-detector workstation test configuration (UDP on 127.0.0.1:9000,
.IR /tmp/daq\-test ,
web view on 127.0.0.1:8001).
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.sh (1)
uses it when no
.B \-\-config
is given.
.TP
.I events.db
SQLite database, at
.B storage.options.path
resolved against the current working directory.
Tables
.B downtime_events
and
.BR detector_state_log .
Timestamps are stored as UTC wall\-clock strings without an offset.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The application reads no environment variables of its own.
Qt honours
.B DISPLAY
and
.BR QT_QPA_PLATFORM ;
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen
runs it without a display (used by the test suite).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit through the tray
.I Quit
action, the window manager, or
.BR SIGINT .
.TP
.B 1
Configuration error (missing
.B storage
or
.B metric
section, no detectors, duplicate detector id, unloadable plugin) or a
failure to bind the web server port; a Python traceback is printed.
.TP
.B 2
Command\-line usage error.
.TP
.B 143
Terminated by
.BR SIGTERM .
No handler is installed for
.BR SIGTERM ,
so the process exits without stopping detector threads, without closing the
storage backend and without closing an open downtime event; that event stays
open in the database and is not reattached on the next start.
Use
.B SIGINT
for a clean stop.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the workstation test configuration in the foreground:
.PP
.RS
.nf
source venv/bin/activate
mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger \-\-config config/local.yaml \-\-log\-level DEBUG
.fi
.RE
.PP
Drive it from a second terminal with the diagnostic tools:
.PP
.RS
.nf
python \-m tools.udp_broadcast \-\-host 127.0.0.1 \-\-port 9000 \-\-state running
python \-m tools.disk_writer \-\-path /tmp/daq\-test \-\-interval 5
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run headless, for example under a test harness:
.PP
.RS
.nf
QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger \-c config/local.yaml
.fi
.RE
